"""Long-form article — Best Running Boards, Side Steps & Rock Sliders for 2010–2024 Toyota 4Runner (5th gen, N280).
No invented hands-on testing: fit facts come from the Amazon listing titles recorded in FITS (found 2026-10-05 through
amazon.com-restricted searches) and from the maker fit lists in sources; specs come from the maker and retailer pages
in sources (read 2026-10-05 through a text extraction, so the page attributes rather than quotes).
Read by listing title only, and worded that way in the text: both TAC picks, the APS boards and the extra TAC and
Hooke Road rows in FITS (no maker page opened). Hooke Road's own page HE.9801-S was read for the tube sliders; the
Amazon listing's part number could not be matched to it and the text says so.
Trim limits in cond_dict come from listing titles only. Rough Country's and Cali Raised's Amazon titles name no grade,
so their cond_dict is {} and the maker's exclusions (Rough Country: not Limited, 2010–2013 SR5 or TRD Sport; Cali
Raised: not Limited or TRD Sport unless X-REAS and side moldings are removed) are in the FITS note and the text.
Not verified, and worded as such in the text: why makers split the Limited, Nightshade, TRD Sport and 2010–2013 SR5
from the other grades (Toyota's releases do not say); whether running boards or automatic running boards were standard
or optional on a given grade and year (Toyota's 2013 release: newly available on SR5 and Limited; Toyota's 2023
brochure lists them by grade, and the extraction's standard/optional labels were not relied on); whether any pick goes
on with factory boards in place; load ratings other than Rough Country's; 2010–2013 Trail and SR5 fit of Westin
56-13835 (Amazon title says 2010–2024 Trail Edition, Westin's list starts both at 2014); 2010–2013 SR5 fit of Westin
21-23585 (in the Amazon title, not on Westin's list); Nightshade years (Westin 2020–2021, TAC titles 2019–2022 and
2020–2021, Wikipedia from 2019). No owner forum was opened, so no owner reports are cited beyond etrailer's reviewer notes.
Not found in an amazon.com result whose title names this vehicle and a 2010–2024 year, and therefore not on the page:
AMP Research PowerStep, N-Fab (titles say only "for Toyota 4Runner"), Go Rhino RB10/RB20 (titles name no vehicle).
"""

