FAQ = [
 ("Do running boards for a 4Runner SR5 fit the Limited?",
  "Usually not. Makers and sellers split the 2010–2024 4Runner into two groups. Westin lists its PRO TRAXX 4 bars 21-23585 for the 2010–2024 Limited, the 2020–2021 Nightshade and the 2022–2023 TRD Sport, and its HDX Drop 56-13835 for the SR5 from 2014, the Trail, TRD Off-Road, TRD Pro and Venture. Rough Country says its power boards do not fit the Limited, the 2010–2013 SR5 or the TRD Sport. TAC and Hooke Road print the same exclusions in their Amazon titles. Find your grade and model year in the title or in the maker's fit list before you order anything."),
 ("Why is the 2010–2013 SR5 grouped with the Limited?",
  "We could not confirm the reason from Toyota. What we can report is how the parts are listed. Amazon titles for Westin's PRO TRAXX bars and TAC's aluminum boards put the 2010–2013 SR5 with the Limited, and Rough Country, TAC and Hooke Road exclude the 2010–2013 SR5 from parts made for the later SR5 and the TRD grades. Westin's own fit list for the HDX Drop starts the SR5 at 2014. Wikipedia dates the 4Runner's facelift to the 2014 model year. If you own a 2010–2013 SR5, treat it as its own case and buy only a part whose title names it."),
 ("Did my 4Runner come with factory running boards?",
  "It may have. Toyota's 2013 release says the SR5 and Limited offer newly available automatic running boards. Toyota's 2023 brochure lists running boards among the packages and options for the SR5, SR5 Premium, TRD Sport, TRD Off-Road, TRD Off-Road Premium, Limited and TRD Pro, and automatic running boards for the TRD Sport and Limited. We could not confirm from the text we read which of these were standard on a given grade, or the list for every model year. Look under the doors. If boards are already there, ask the seller whether the new part goes on in their place and what has to come off first."),
 ("Do 2010–2024 4Runner running boards fit the 2025–2026 4Runner?",
  "No. The 2025 4Runner is a new generation. Wikipedia says it was revealed on April 9, 2024 and is based on the same body-on-frame platform as the Tacoma, and makers sell separate parts for it. Rough Country, for example, has nerf steps titled for the 2025–2026 4Runner. Every pick on this page names the 2010–2024 body. If you are shopping for the new model, use a listing that names 2025 or later, and do not assume the brackets from the old body carry over. The reverse also holds: skip any listing whose title names only 2025 and later."),
 ("Are power running boards worth it on a 4Runner?",
  "They cost the most and they solve a real conflict. Toyota's 2020 release gives 9.6 in of ground clearance on four-wheel-drive models, and a fixed step hangs below the rocker all the time. A power board drops when a door opens and tucks under the rocker when it closes. Rough Country lists its dual-motor kit at $1,399.95 on its own site, with 6 in aluminum boards, LED lights and a 660 lb rating per side. That is more than twice Westin's list price for the HDX Drop. Rough Country says the kit does not fit the Limited, the 2010–2013 SR5 or the TRD Sport, so check your grade first."),
 ("Running boards or rock sliders: which does a 4Runner need?",
  "It depends on what the rocker panel will meet. A running board or nerf bar is a step. It bolts on with light brackets and is not built to carry the vehicle. A rock slider is armor. Cali Raised's Step Edition uses 1.75 in DOM tubing with a .120 in wall and full frame plates, weighs about 90 lb a set, and has a flat top so it also works as a step. For pavement and gravel, a step is cheaper and lower to climb on. For rocky trails, a slider protects the rocker and gives a step that sits higher. Never jack the vehicle on a running board."),
 ("Do I need to drill to install 4Runner running boards?",
  "Not for the parts whose maker pages we read. Westin says the HDX Drop and PRO TRAXX 4 need no drilling on most applications, and etrailer describes the HDX Drop 56-13835 as bolting to existing holes. Rough Country calls its power boards an easy no-drill installation. Cali Raised describes its sliders as 100 percent bolt-on with no drilling or cutting, and Hooke Road says its tube sliders use factory bolts and stock connecting points. Power boards still need wiring, and Cali Raised says 2010–2013 models need a trim panel at the rocker removed first. For the two TAC listings, confirm on the listing."),
 ("Do rock sliders fit a 4Runner with KDSS or X-REAS?",
  "Cali Raised says its Step Edition sliders are compatible with both KDSS and non-KDSS models. Toyota's 2020 release lists KDSS as available on the TRD Off-Road. X-REAS is the other system to know. Toyota's 2020 release calls it exclusive to the Limited, and the 2023 brochure lists it on the TRD Sport and Limited. Cali Raised says its sliders are not compatible with Limited or TRD Sport models unless X-REAS and the side moldings are removed, and Rough Country says models with X-REAS need a controller bracket modification for its power boards. Hooke Road's page mentions neither system, so ask the seller."),
 ("How much weight can 4Runner running boards hold?",
  "Only one pick publishes a figure that we read: Rough Country rates its power boards at 660 lb per side. Westin's pages for the HDX Drop and PRO TRAXX 4 give no load rating, and neither does etrailer's page for the HDX Drop. Cali Raised and Hooke Road publish tube sizes but no step rating. The two TAC listings were read by title only. If a heavy rider will use the step, or you plan to stand on it to load the roof, ask the seller for a per-side rating in writing before you order, and do not treat a missing number as a high one."),
 ("Will steel side steps rust on a 4Runner?",
  "They can. Westin's HDX Drop 56-13835 is powder-coated steel. etrailer's page for it carries reviewer reports of rust within one to two years and a customer service reply saying the 3-year warranty does not cover rust. Westin also sells a stainless version, 56-138352, with a 5-year warranty. Its PRO TRAXX 4 bars are e-coated steel under black powder coat with a 3-year warranty, and polished 304 stainless PRO TRAXX bars carry a lifetime warranty. In salt states, rinse the steps and brackets through winter and touch up chips early. Aluminum boards do not rust, though road salt can still corrode them."),
]

